     "display": true
    },
    {
     "p": "$$= \\frac{1}{3^{4}}\\text{ tan }\\theta + \\frac{tan^{3} \\theta}{3} + c$$",
     "display": true
    },
    {
     "p": "We know that $\\frac{x+2}{3} =$ sin $\\theta$ . Sketch a right triangle whose opposite side has length $x +2$ and whose hypotenuse has length 3. Applying the Pythagorean theorem, we see that tan $\\theta = \\frac{x + 2}{\\sqrt{5 - 4x - x^{2}}}$. Therefore,"
    },
